module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GradedAlgebraPushPull
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.RingedSpace.ModuleUnitEpi

/-!
# The unit of the graded push–pull adjunction is degreewise the unit on modules

`Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra.pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction` makes the pullback of
sheaves of graded algebras along a morphism of ringed spaces left adjoint to the pushforward. Its
unit at a sheaf of graded `𝒪_Y`-algebras `A` is a **homomorphism of sheaves of graded algebras**

`η_A : A ⟶ f_* f^* A`,

and it is the only candidate for the canonical surjection `⨁_n A_n ⟶ ⨁_n f_*f^*A_n` that the graded
arguments of [Stacks Project, Tag 09MS] use: by construction it respects the multiplication and the
unit, so none of that has to be checked.

What this file adds is the one identification that makes it usable: **in each degree `n` the
component of `η_A` is the unit of the adjunction on sheaves of modules at `A_n`**
(`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportAdjunction_unit_app_app` in general,
`Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra.pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction_unit_app_app` for a
morphism of ringed spaces). Without it the graded unit is opaque, and nothing known about the
module-level unit — its epimorphy under [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3] part (1), or the computation of
its kernel as `ℐ A_n` — can be transported to it. With it, both transfer degreewise and on the
nose, because `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transport_piece` is `rfl`.

The identification is forced, not chosen: the unit of an adjunction built by
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.mkOfHomEquiv` is the hom-set bijection applied to the identity, and the
hom-set bijection of `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportAdjunction` is degreewise the hom-set
bijection of the underlying adjunction (`transportAdjunction_homEquiv`).

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportAdjunction_unit_app_app`: the degree-`n` component of the
  unit of the transported adjunction is the unit of the underlying monoidal adjunction at the
  degree-`n` piece.
* `Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra.pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction_unit_app_app`: the
  same for pullback and pushforward along a morphism of ringed spaces.
* `Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra.epi_gradedUnit_app_of_generatingSections`: **the local
  surjectivity of the graded unit, degree by degree.** For a morphism of ringed spaces whose
  comorphism on modules is an epimorphism and whose pushforward of modules is a left adjoint — the
  two properties of a closed immersion that
  `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_of_generatingSections` takes — the degree-`n`
  component of `η_A` is an epimorphism as soon as `A_n` is generated by global sections.

## What is not done

**Nothing here is about a line bundle, and no `stacks` attribute is attached.** The hypothesis of
the last result is global generation of the piece, which is what [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3] part
(1) is proved under in this repository
(`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_of_generatingSections`); for the pieces `L^{⊗ n}` of the
symmetric algebra of an invertible module that hypothesis is *not* automatic, and the general
statement of Tag 01R3 — epimorphy of the unit at an arbitrary sheaf of modules along a closed
immersion, which is a local statement and holds because a module is locally a quotient of a free
one — is not available in either tree. So the graded unit is here exhibited, and its degreewise
surjectivity is reduced to exactly the module-level input, but it is not asserted unconditionally.

## Implementation notes

**The ring sheaf is spelled `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat`.** The statements below are written
over `toRingCat J Osharp` and `toRingCat K Psharp` rather than over
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Osharp` and `… Psharp`, and the two spellings are equal by
`rfl`. The choice is forced all the same, and what forces it is the hypothesis `[L.Monoidal]`.
`Stacks.TensorSheafWorld.monoidalCategory` (`TensorSheafWorldBridge.lean:256`) is the only
`MonoidalCategory (SheafOfModules.{w} _)` whose universe `w` of sections is free of the two sites'
universes, and it is named at the `toRingCat` spelling alone; the two spellings are different
`DiscrTree` keys, since `ringSheaf` reduces to an application of `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose` and
no further, so an instance registered at one is invisible at the other.

The monoidal structures that *are* stated at the `ringSheaf` spelling —
`SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryRingSheaf` (`Monoidal.lean:190`) and
`SheafOfModules.monoidalCategorySheafTensor` (`MonoidalSheafTensor.lean:293`) — pin both the ring
universe and the module universe to `max u v`, which the free `w` of the statements below cannot
match: the first of them is found as soon as the module universe is specialized to `max u₁ v₁`, and
not before. Restating this file over `ringSheaf` therefore waits on
`Stacks.TensorSheafWorld.monoidalCategory` being stated there with `w` free, which is a change to
that file rather than to this one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FQX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FQX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01R3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0096](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0096)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory CategoryTheory.Sheaf PresheafOfModules AlgebraicGeometry
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction Stacks.RingedSpace Stacks.PullbackMonoidalSheaf
open Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra

universe v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ u w

namespace SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra

section Adjunction

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  {Osharp : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] {K : GrothendieckTopology D}
  [K.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  {Psharp : Sheaf K CommRingCat.{w}}
  [K.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify K AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

attribute [local instance] Stacks.TensorSheafWorld.monoidalCategory

variable {L : SheafOfModules.{w} (toRingCat K Psharp) ⥤ SheafOfModules.{w} (toRingCat J Osharp)}
  {G : SheafOfModules.{w} (toRingCat J Osharp) ⥤ SheafOfModules.{w} (toRingCat K Psharp)}
  (adj : L ⊣ G) [L.Monoidal] [G.LaxMonoidal] [adj.IsMonoidal]
  (hO : Presheaf.IsSheaf J
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf Osharp.obj))
  (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf K
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf Psharp.obj))

include hO hP

/-- **The unit of the transported adjunction is, in each degree, the unit of the underlying
adjunction at that degree's piece.**

The unit of an adjunction presented by `CategoryTheory.Adjunction.mkOfHomEquiv` is the hom-set
bijection applied to the identity, and
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportAdjunction_homEquiv` says that bijection is degreewise the
hom-set bijection of `adj`. Both sides are typed by
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transport_piece`, which is `rfl`. -/
theorem transportAdjunction_unit_app_app (B : GradedAlgebra.{w, w} (toRingCat K Psharp)) (n : ℤ) :
    ((transportAdjunction adj hO hP).unit.app B).app n = adj.unit.app (B.piece n) := by
  rw [← (transportAdjunction adj hO hP).homEquiv_id B]
  simp only [transportAdjunction_homEquiv]
  exact adj.homEquiv_id (B.piece n)

end Adjunction

end SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra

namespace Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra

variable {X Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

attribute [local instance] Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra.pullbackStrictMonoidal pushforwardFunctorLaxMonoidal

/-- **The canonical homomorphism of sheaves of graded algebras `A ⟶ f_* f^* A`**: the unit of
`Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra.pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction`. Being a unit it is
multiplicative by construction; it is **not** unital by construction, because
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Hom` carries no unit law and the hom-set bijection of
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportAdjunction` makes no claim about the distinguished
degree-zero unit. The unit law is a theorem,
`Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra.gradedUnitUnitalHom`. -/
noncomputable def gradedUnit (A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf Y)) :
    A ⟶ (SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportFunctor (pushforwardFunctor f)
        (structureSheafRing X).property (structureSheafRing Y).property).obj
      ((SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportFunctor (pullbackFunctor f)
        (structureSheafRing Y).property (structureSheafRing X).property).obj A) :=
  (pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction f).unit.app A

/-- **The degree-`n` component of `A ⟶ f_* f^* A` is the unit of `f^* ⊣ f_*` on sheaves of modules
at `A_n`.** -/
theorem pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction_unit_app_app
    (A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf Y)) (n : ℤ) :
    (gradedUnit f A).app n =
      (modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app (A.piece n) :=
  SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.transportAdjunction_unit_app_app (pullbackAdjunction f)
    (structureSheafRing X).property (structureSheafRing Y).property A n

/-- **The local surjectivity of `A ⟶ f_* f^* A`, degree by degree.** Under the two properties of
`f` that `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_of_generatingSections` takes — epimorphy of the
comorphism on modules and the pushforward of modules being a left adjoint, both of which a closed
immersion of ringed spaces has — the degree-`n` component of the graded unit is an epimorphism as
soon as `A_n` is generated by global sections.

This is [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3] part (1) read on a sheaf of graded algebras, and it is the
statement the graded arguments of [Stacks Project, Tag 09MS] need about
`⨁_n A_n ⟶ ⨁_n f_* f^* A_n`: that the map is surjective locally in each degree. -/
theorem epi_gradedUnit_app_of_generatingSections [Epi (structureSheafModuleHom f)]
    [(modulePushforward f).IsLeftAdjoint]
    (A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf Y)) (n : ℤ)
    (σ : (A.piece n).GeneratingSections) :
    Epi ((gradedUnit f A).app n) := by
  rw [pullbackPushforwardGradedAlgebraAdjunction_unit_app_app f A n]
  exact epi_unit_app_of_generatingSections f σ

end Stacks.PushforwardGradedAlgebra

end
